## Solution
I continued investigating the prompt construction and ultimately solved the challenge.
---

## Key Takeaways

- Text that looks like a system or assistant message is not necessarily a real system or assistant message.
- Prompt construction becomes dangerous when security boundaries are represented only by text.
- AI applications should separate trusted instructions from untrusted user content structurally rather than relying solely on textual delimiters.
- Error messages and model responses can sometimes reveal useful information about the underlying prompt structure.
